%e A397211 a(3)=8 because M(8)=0, M(9)=1, M(10)=1, and there is no prior run of 3 nonnegative Moebius terms.
%o A397211 (C) // See Links
%o A397211 (PARI) a(n) = {my(k=0, r=0); while(r<n, k++; if(moebius(k)>=0, r++, r=0)); k-r+1} \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 02 2026
